#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 804pt, "C Trivedi ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 27.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 98.16pt, "Numerical investigation of unsteady flow ")
  #line-at(72pt, 130.454pt, "in a reversible pump-turbine ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 14.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#707070"))
  #line-at(72pt, 153.48pt, "Chirag Trivedi ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 182.76pt, "Associate Professor, Waterpower Laboratory, Department of Energy and Process Engineering, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 195.357pt, "NTNU—Norwegian University of Science and Technology, Alfred Getz' vei. 4, 7491 Trondheim, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 208.075pt, "Norway. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 220.671pt, "Email: chirag.trivedi@ntnu.no ")
  #line-at(72pt, 245.986pt, "Friday, 23 January 2026 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 288.72pt, "ABSTRACT")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 301.08pt, "Pump-turbine type hydraulic turbine is widely used to mitigate the intermittent energy demand and ")
  #line-at(72pt, 313.798pt, "store a large-scale energy. Flow conditions in turbine mode and pump mode operations is substantially ")
  #line-at(72pt, 326.395pt, "different. A computational model of the pump-turbine was created, and the model included hexahedral ")
  #line-at(72.011pt, 338.991pt, "mesh of 58.19 million nodes. Total verification and validation error was 7.7%. Three operating ")
  #line-at(72.011pt, 351.709pt, "conditions in turbine mode and four in pump mode were simulated. Flow characteristics, such as ")
  #line-at(72.011pt, 364.306pt, "blade loading, time-dependent pressure fluctuations, frequency spectra, radial and tangential velocity ")
  #line-at(72.011pt, 377.024pt, "were investigated. The frequency spectra revealed amplitude of frequencies up to tenth harmonics of ")
  #line-at(72.011pt, 389.621pt, "the blade passing frequency in pump mode. The higher harmonic frequencies can potentially reach the ")
  #line-at(72.011pt, 402.217pt, "high mode eigen frequencies and increase the risk of resonance. Flow field analysis in the draft tube ")
  #line-at(72.011pt, 414.935pt, "indicted the strong presence of Dean vortices causing highly asymmetric flow at the runner inlet in ")
  #line-at(72.011pt, 427.532pt, "pump mode operation. ")
  #line-at(72.011pt, 452.847pt, "Keywords: CFD; Energy; Hydropower; Pump-turbine; Turbine; Simulations. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 20.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#003b57"))
  #line-at(72pt, 492.12pt, "Introduction ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 522.12pt, "Annual CO2 emission has reached 42 billion tonnes and increases continuously. The trajectory has ")
  #line-at(72pt, 541.076pt, "been largely parabolic since the year 1900, the annual CO2 emission was around one billion tonnes. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 560.153pt, "China, North America and Europe account for 53%, 18% and 17% of global emissions in recent years, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 579.109pt, "respectively. The impact of CO2 and greenhouse gases on climate is clearly visible. To minimize the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 598.064pt, "impact, the concept of energy mix is being implemented worldwide, and the share of renewable ")
  #line-at(72pt, 617.02pt, "energy has been steadily increasing from 18% in the year 2000 to 30% in 2023. The wind and solar ")
  #line-at(72pt, 635.976pt, "energy integration is reached to 1000 GW in recent years. On the other hand, to provide stable energy ")
  #line-at(72pt, 654.931pt, "to the consumers, flexibility and grid balance are essential. The gas turbine and hydropower plants ")
  #line-at(72pt, 673.887pt, "play pivotal role to mitigate intermittency, from the wind and solar energy, and balance the power ")
  #line-at(72pt, 692.843pt, "grid. The major limitation for the gas turbine power plant is the emission of carbon dioxide, nitrogen ")
  #line-at(72pt, 711.798pt, "oxide and other organic compounds. The emission is high during the grid balance where the turbines ")
  #line-at(72pt, 730.875pt, "operate at off design loads and results in abnormal combustion. Hydropower is recognized as a ")
  #line-at(72pt, 749.831pt, "valuable alternative energy source due to its substantially lower emissions. The global energy ")
]

// arXiv source page 2
#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 804pt, "C Trivedi ")
  #line-at(72pt, 82.315pt, "production from hydropower is around 12 000 TWh. The hydropower provides high flexibility, and it ")
  #line-at(72pt, 101.271pt, "can operate in tandem with solar and wind power generators. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 128.275pt, "Reversible pump-turbine is an essential component of an energy storage type hydropower plant. The ")
  #line-at(72pt, 147.23pt, "pump-turbine generates electricity in turbine mode and store energy in pump mode operations ")
  #line-at(72pt, 166.186pt, "depending on requirement. Therefore, the pump-turbine plays critical role in the energy system to ")
  #line-at(72pt, 185.142pt, "mitigate flexibility. The rotational direction is opposite in pump mode and the water flows in reverse ")
  #line-at(72pt, 204.097pt, "direction, i.e., from the lower reservoir to the upper reservoir. The pump-turbine is integrated with ")
  #line-at(72pt, 223.053pt, "other valuable components, such as, spiral casing to guide the water, stay vanes to distribute the water ")
  #line-at(72pt, 242.13pt, "circumferentially, guide vanes to control the water flow through the turbine, runner to extract energy ")
  #line-at(72pt, 261.086pt, "from the water, and draft turbine to recover the pressure energy. Modern pump-turbines have achieved ")
  #line-at(72.011pt, 280.042pt, "the efficiency up to 94% both turbine and pump mode operations at design load [1]. However, at off ")
  #line-at(72.011pt, 298.997pt, "design loads the efficiency is low, a round-trip efficiency drops below 50%. There are several ")
  #line-at(72.011pt, 317.953pt, "challenges to operate pump-turbine at off-design loads [2], however, the key challenge corresponds to ")
  #line-at(72.022pt, 336.909pt, "the unsteady vortex breakdown and the resulting dynamic instability [3]. Therefore, the operating ")
  #line-at(72.022pt, 355.864pt, "range is restricted and, as a result, the limited scope for mitigating the energy flexibility. ")
  #line-at(72.022pt, 382.868pt, "At design load, flow separation is minimal in the blade channel as the guide vane outlet angle, and the ")
  #line-at(72.022pt, 401.824pt, "blade inlet angle are well aligned. At high load and part load conditions, the flow angles are skewed ")
  #line-at(72.022pt, 420.78pt, "and induce asymmetric flow to the blade leading edge. This results in flow separation around the ")
  #line-at(72.022pt, 439.735pt, "leading edge, and the separation grows as flow travels further downstream in the blade channel. ")
  #line-at(72.022pt, 458.691pt, "Furthermore, angular rotation of the turbine runner, induce additional effect on the flow causing ")
  #line-at(72.022pt, 477.768pt, "inception of vortical flow and the local swirls. ")
  #line-at(72.022pt, 504.651pt, "Reversible pump-turbine is stable and works well around the design load [4–7]. There is moderate ")
  #line-at(72.033pt, 523.606pt, "impact on the turbine due to interaction between the rotating component (runner/impeller) and the ")
  #line-at(72.033pt, 542.683pt, "stationary component (guide vanes and stay vanes). This rotor-stator interaction is investigated by the ")
  #line-at(72.033pt, 561.639pt, "researchers [8,9] and, generally, the turbines withstand this type of repetitive dynamic loads at design ")
  #line-at(72.033pt, 580.595pt, "condition. At off-design load, the turbine experiences challenges, high pressure amplitudes from ")
  #line-at(72.033pt, 599.55pt, "vortex breakdown in the blade channel, draft tube and vaneless space [10–12].  ")
  #line-at(72.033pt, 626.554pt, "The blade channels are subjected to different categories of vortical flow, depending on the operating ")
  #line-at(72.033pt, 645.51pt, "conditions of the reversible pump-turbine. So far, the emphasize has been placed on the s-curve ")
  #line-at(72.033pt, 664.466pt, "characteristics and the rotating stall. However, inception of vortical flow during other operating ")
  #line-at(72.033pt, 683.421pt, "conditions is major challenge due to loss of efficiency, and it is not clearly understood, specifically ")
  #line-at(72.033pt, 702.377pt, "off-design loads. Furthermore, there is no or very limited study on the pump mode operation of the ")
  #line-at(72.033pt, 721.333pt, "turbine. The flow field in the blade channel is significantly different from that of the turbine mode. ")
  #line-at(72.033pt, 740.288pt, "This study aims to investigate the unsteady flow in the vaneless space and runner blade channel of the ")
  #line-at(72.033pt, 759.244pt, "reversible pump-turbine at wide operating range. The study encapsulates both modes of operation, i.e., ")
]

