  #line-at(71.998pt, 120.231pt, "SST) is an optimal turbulence modelling approach, taking the benefit of local fine mesh and ")
  #line-at(71.998pt, 139.187pt, "dynamically adjusts the resolved length scales, Artificial Forcing function and adjusting the von ")
  #line-at(71.998pt, 158.143pt, "Karman length scale. A detailed information about the mathematical model of SAS-SST is available ")
  #line-at(71.998pt, 177.22pt, "in the literature [22,23]. SAS tends to an explicit transfer of kinetic energy, where the flow ")
  #line-at(71.998pt, 196.176pt, "instabilities are not at the level of LES requirement. SAS uses forcing terms in the momentum ")
  #line-at(71.998pt, 215.131pt, "equation to convert into resolved kinetic energy from the modelled kinetic energy [23]. SAS-SST ")
  #line-at(71.998pt, 234.087pt, "model has demonstrated the success of modelling the complex flow conditions in hydraulic turbines ")
  #line-at(71.998pt, 253.043pt, "including the reversible pump-turbine [11,24,25].  ")
