  #line-at(71.991pt, 635.524pt, "Given the available computational resources and suitability for hydraulic turbines, the SAS–SST ")
  #line-at(71.991pt, 654.479pt, "turbulence model was selected as the optimal approach for this study. All unsteady simulations were ")
  #line-at(71.991pt, 673.435pt, "therefore performed using the SAS–SST turbulence model. The selected time-step size for the present ")
  #line-at(71.991pt, 692.391pt, "study was one degree of runner rotation. The researchers [9,25–30] used 0.5 – 2 degree time-step size ")
  #line-at(71.991pt, 711.347pt, "depending on requirement for the residual convergence. The simulations were performed for a total of ")
  #line-at(71.991pt, 730.302pt, "10 revolutions of the runner at each operating points to ensure converged flow field. The General Grid ")
  #line-at(71.991pt, 749.379pt, "Interface between the rotating and stationary domain was modelled as transient rotor-stator interface. ")
]

