#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-15.png", width: 337pt), 72pt, 508.5pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 804pt, "C Trivedi ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 14.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#003b57"))
  #line-at(72pt, 85.2pt, "Blade loading ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 110.52pt, "Runner is a rotating component of the turbine, and the flow field is largely dependent on the incoming ")
  #line-at(72pt, 129.476pt, "flow angle (guide vane angular position), available vaneless space, angular speed of the runner, and ")
  #line-at(72pt, 148.431pt, "blade design. Runner blades extract the potential and kinetic energy of water and deliver lift ")
  #line-at(72pt, 167.387pt, "(mechanical torque). Blade loading shows the energy extractions from the leading edge to the trailing ")
  #line-at(72pt, 186.343pt, "edge. Pump-turbine runner blades are different from that of the Francis turbine. Pump-turbine blades ")
  #line-at(72pt, 205.298pt, "are designed to extract energy and deliver torque in turbine mode, while they use torque and deliver ")
  #line-at(72pt, 224.254pt, "energy (head) in pump mode. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(204.48pt, 224.254pt, "Figure 11")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(248.64pt, 224.254pt, " shows blade loading for ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(359.515pt, 224.254pt, "α")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(365.28pt, 225.24pt, "t")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(367.2pt, 224.28pt, " = 1 and 1.18 in turbine mode. The ")
  #line-at(72.001pt, 243.236pt, "chord (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(103.565pt, 243.236pt, "l/c")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(114.483pt, 243.236pt, ") length 0 and 1 represents the leading and trailing edges, respectively. The pressure values ")
  #line-at(72.001pt, 262.191pt, "are extracted at the mid-span of the blade and normalized by specific hydraulic energy. Large part of ")
  #line-at(72.001pt, 281.268pt, "the energy is extracted by the first half part of the chord. Overall trend of the pressure loading is ")
  #line-at(72.001pt, 300.224pt, "almost similar, except for the pressure values for part load, design load, and high load. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(454.602pt, 300.224pt, "Figure 12")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.001pt, 319.18pt, "shows the contours of the pressure loading on the blades. We can see high and low pressure on the ")
  #line-at(72.001pt, 338.136pt, "leading edge, pressure side, and suction side, respectively. Pressure distribution across the span from ")
  #line-at(72.001pt, 357.091pt, "the hub to the shroud is uniform. Overall pressure reduces along the chord of the blade, and we can ")
  #line-at(72.001pt, 376.047pt, "see low pressure (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(151.202pt, 376.047pt, "p/ρE")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(171.847pt, 376.047pt, " = 0.03) on the trailing edge. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(299.886pt, 376.047pt, "Figure 13")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(344.645pt, 376.047pt, " shows the velocity contours at 95% and ")
  #line-at(72.001pt, 395.003pt, "5% span of the runner. The span 95% and 5% is near to the hub and shroud of the runner. Flow ")
  #line-at(72.001pt, 413.958pt, "separation and secondary flow around the leading edge can be seen. The separation results in a small ")
  #line-at(72.001pt, 432.914pt, "swirling zone near to the leading edge. However, the swirling zone diffuses further downstream in the ")
