#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-36.png", width: 4pt), 90.5pt, 114pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 804pt, "C Trivedi ")
  #line-at(108.001pt, 82.315pt, "draft tube elbow axis. The Dean vortices draw momentum from the outer edge swirl and mix ")
  #line-at(108.001pt, 101.271pt, "with the core swirl. ")
  #line-at(108.012pt, 120.227pt, "The blade pressure loading increases from the trailing edge to the leading edge. ")
  #line-at(108.024pt, 139.182pt, "Frequency spectra in the runner revealed high amplitude and wide band low frequencies ")
  #line-at(108.024pt, 158.138pt, "indicating a complex and stochastic flow field. Furthermore, the spectra show frequencies of ")
  #line-at(108.024pt, 177.215pt, "runner rotation, guide vane passing, and the blade passing. Presence of blade passing ")
  #line-at(108.024pt, 196.171pt, "frequency in the runner is uncommon. ")
  #line-at(108.024pt, 215.126pt, "Contour of velocity field revealed several vortical zones and inter-blade vortices in the blade ")
  #line-at(108.023pt, 234.082pt, "channel. ")
  #line-at(108.035pt, 253.038pt, "Flow field in the vaneless space, guide vane passage, and the stay vane passage revealed ")
  #line-at(108.035pt, 271.994pt, "strong interactions among the blade leading edge vortex shedding and the guide vane trailing ")
  #line-at(108.035pt, 290.949pt, "edge stagnation point. Furthermore, a vortex of high radial velocity travels through the guide ")
  #line-at(108.035pt, 309.905pt, "vanes and interacts with the leading edge wake of the guide vanes. ")
  #line-at(72.033pt, 338.94pt, "The frequency spectra in the guide vanes showed amplitudes of frequencies up to tenth harmonics of ")
  #line-at(72.033pt, 357.896pt, "the blade passing frequency, indicating the strong presence of rotor-stator interaction frequencies in ")
  #line-at(72.033pt, 376.852pt, "the turbine. The frequencies can potentially align with the higher mode eigen frequencies and induce ")
  #line-at(72.033pt, 395.807pt, "resonance. The combination of guide vane passing frequency, blade passing frequency (higher ")
  #line-at(72.033pt, 414.763pt, "harmonics), runner rotational frequency, and the eigen frequency potentially results in strong flow-")
  #line-at(72.033pt, 433.719pt, "induced resonance in the turbine and eventually fatigue failure. ")
